Arrow Flow: Privacy Policy

Last updated: 16 November 2026
App: Arrow Flow: Arrow Puzzle Game (com.bosscodes.arrowflow)
Developer: BossCodes
Contact: hassamarain797@gmail.com

Arrow Flow is a puzzle game for Android. This policy explains, in plain words, what the
app does with your information. The short version: the game keeps your progress on your
phone and has no account of its own. Two Google services are used: Google Play Games,
only if you choose to sign in, to keep your progress safe (section 4), and Google AdMob,
which shows the ads and uses your Advertising ID (section 5).

1. What we collect

We do not ask for your name, e-mail address, phone number, contacts, photos, microphone,
camera or location, the game has no account of its own, and we run no analytics or
tracking of our own. We do not store your information on any server of ours, and we do
not sell it. Two things involve Google:

Signing in to Google Play Games is optional and saves your progress to your own Play
Games account (section 4).
Arrow Flow shows ads through Google AdMob, which collects some information to show
and measure ads (section 5).
2. What stays on your phone

To let you carry on where you stopped, the game saves on your device: your progress
(levels completed, stars, best times), your streak and records, the golden arrows and
worlds you unlocked, your hints and hearts, and your settings (sound, music, vibration,
dark mode, colours). This data stays on your phone unless you sign in to Google Play
Games (section 4). It is deleted from the phone when you uninstall the app or clear its
storage in Android settings.

3. Internet

The game works offline. It uses the internet only to load ads, to save and restore your
progress if you signed in to Google Play Games, and, if you installed it from Google Play,
for Google Play’s update check. Without signing in to Google Play Games, the app does not
send your game progress anywhere.

4. Google Play Games (optional cloud save)

You can sign in to Google Play Games from Settings. If you do, Arrow Flow saves your
progress (levels, stars, golden arrows, worlds, hints, hearts and your daily gift) as a
“saved game” in your own Google Play Games account, so you can carry on after reinstalling
or on a new phone. The app reads your Play Games player name only to show a letter in
Settings. The saved game and your player ID are handled by Google under Google’s privacy
policy (https://policies.google.com/privacy). We do not receive them on any server of
ours and we do not share them. Your phone settings (sound, dark mode and so on) are not
uploaded.

You are in control. In Settings > Google Play Games you can turn cloud save off
(Disconnect), save now, and Delete my cloud save, which removes the saved game from
your Play Games account. Signing out of Google Play Games itself is done in the Play
Games app. If you never sign in, nothing is saved to the cloud.

5. Ads (Google AdMob)

The game is free and shows ads: a short ad when the app opens or returns to the front, an
ad between screens or levels, and optional videos you can watch to earn a heart or to
continue a level. The ads are provided by Google AdMob. To show them, Google may collect
and use your device’s Advertising ID, approximate location (from your IP address),
information about how you interact with the ads, and device and diagnostic information
(such as crashes), under Google’s privacy policy
(https://policies.google.com/privacy and
https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites). We do not receive your personal
information from this, and we do not sell it.

Your choices:

In the EU, the UK and some other places the game first asks for your consent (Google’s
consent form). You can change your choice at any time in Settings > Privacy options
(it appears where the law asks for it).
On your phone you can reset your Advertising ID or turn off ad personalisation in the
Google settings (Settings > Google > Ads).
Ads shown are limited to content suitable for a general audience.
6. Google Play

If you installed Arrow Flow from Google Play, Google may tell the app that a newer version
is available (the “update available” box) through Google Play’s own update service. This
is done by Google Play on your phone, under Google’s own privacy policy
(https://policies.google.com/privacy). Google Play may also give us anonymous crash and
performance reports (Android vitals) if you chose to share diagnostics with Google; they
contain no personal information about you and we use them only to fix problems.

7. Third-party code and content

The game uses open-source libraries (Flutter, Flame, audioplayers and others) that run
inside the app. Apart from the Google services described above (Google Play Games, Google
AdMob and Google Play), they do not send your data anywhere. The pictures and music in the
game are used under their free licenses; see the credits in the app description and the
project page.

8. Children

Arrow Flow is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
information from children under 13. Ads are set for a general audience. If you think a
child has given us information, write to us and we will remove it.

9. Your choices and rights

We hold no personal information about you on any server of ours, so there is nothing for
us to access, correct or delete. You can remove everything the game saved on your phone at
any time by clearing the app’s storage or uninstalling it. The cloud save can be deleted
in the app (section 4), and for ads you can use the choices in section 5. If you are in
the EU or UK you also have the rights of the GDPR, which you can use with Google as the
provider of the ads and of Google Play Games.

10. Security

Your game data is stored in the app’s private storage on your phone, which other apps
cannot read. Ads and the cloud save are sent over secure connections handled by Google’s
own software.

11. Changes to this policy

If this policy changes (for example when a new feature is added), the new version will be
published at the same address with a new “Last updated” date, and the app description will
mention anything that affects your data.

